# Valgrind suppressions for the valgrind job in native-checks.yaml. tools/
# is .Rbuildignore'd, so nothing here reaches the tarball.
#
# One entry, and the block is R's. do_iconv() (src/main/sysutils.c) fills a
# local R_StringBuffer with R_AllocStringBuffer() and frees it as its last
# statement. When Riconv_open() cannot honour the requested encoding it
# raises error("unsupported conversion ...") from inside its loop, and the
# long jump skips the free. test-parse.R asserts that html_parse(...,
# encoding = "no-such-encoding") is a clean zuhtml_encoding_error, which is
# what provokes it. The same entry is in zuxml, for the same reason.
#
# Matched on the whole call path, so a real leak from any other caller is
# still reported.
{
   R-do_iconv-error-path-skips-R_FreeStringBuffer
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:R_AllocStringBuffer
   fun:do_iconv
}
